            <ArticleTitle>HDL-increasing effect of cyclofenil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nineteen patients with low levels of HDL as measured by APO-AI have been treated with cyclofenil (a non-steroid stilboestrol isomer with very low oestrogenic effects) as the only form of therapy. The therapy elicited a highly significant rise of about 15% in HDL levels. A slight increase in transaminases occurred in 6 patients but was reversible without terminating therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
